{"name":"Royal Coronation","hex":"#3e3542","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"royal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of or relating to a monarch or his (or her) family.","Having the air or demeanour of a monarch; illustrious; magnanimous; of more than common size or excellence."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A royal person; a member of a royal family.","A standard size of printing paper, measuring 25 by 20 inches."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/royal"},{"term":"coronation","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An act of investing with a crown; a crowning.\n\n An act or the ceremony of formally investing a sovereign or the sovereign's consort with a crown and other insignia of royalty, on or shortly after their accession to the sovereignty.","An act or the ceremony of formally investing a sovereign or the sovereign's consort with a crown and other insignia of royalty, on or shortly after their accession to the sovereignty."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/coronation"}],"entries":[{"title":"Coronation","blocks":[{"text":"A coronation ceremony marks the formal investiture of a monarch with regal power using a crown. In addition to the crowning, this ceremony may include the presentation of other items of regalia, and other rituals such as the taking of special vows by the new monarch, the investing and presentation of regalia to them, and acts of homage by the new monarch's subjects. In certain Christian denominations, such as Lutheranism and Anglicanism, coronation is a religious rite. As such, Western-style coronations have often included anointing the monarch with holy oil, or chrism as it is often called; the anointing ritual's religious significance follows examples found in the Bible. The monarch's consort may also be crowned, either simultaneously with the monarch or as a separate event."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Charles-vii-courronement-_Panth%C3%A9on_III.jpg/330px-Charles-vii-courronement-_Panth%C3%A9on_III.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Coronation","wikidata":"Q209715"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Jacob_Axelsson_Lindblom_kr%C3%B6ner_Karl_XIV_Johan.jpg/500px-Jacob_Axelsson_Lindblom_kr%C3%B6ner_Karl_XIV_Johan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Jacob_Axelsson_Lindblom_kr%C3%B6ner_Karl_XIV_Johan.jpg/1280px-Jacob_Axelsson_Lindblom_kr%C3%B6ner_Karl_XIV_Johan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/50/Jacob_Axelsson_Lindblom_kr%C3%B6ner_Karl_XIV_Johan.jpg/500px-Jacob_Axelsson_Lindblom_kr%C3%B6ner_Karl_XIV_Johan.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The coronation of Charles XIV John of Sweden, by Evangelical-Lutheran archbishop Jacob Axelsson Lindblom (1818); detail of the painting by Per Krafft the Younger","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AJacob_Axelsson_Lindblom_kr%C3%B6ner_Karl_XIV_Johan.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Martorana_RogerII2008.jpg/500px-Martorana_RogerII2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Martorana_RogerII2008.jpg/1280px-Martorana_RogerII2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/04/Martorana_RogerII2008.jpg/500px-Martorana_RogerII2008.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Roger II of Sicily receiving his crown directly from Jesus Christ, mosaic from Martorana, Palermo","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMa